{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_bdrk_4qjlsh2fqkt2rmwmrnhrb3yiffkf4u3nkvrer233mti3hs24kp6u","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01wC5yVjhR3ER4I5FWpSPdnN","name":"mcp__figma__use_figma","input":{"fileKey":"7etw0umjivQ6Yi6l5iEkX3","description":"Read all text from Start Here and Foundations pages","code":"const out=[];\nfor (const id of ['0:1','1:2']) {\n  const p = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(id);\n  await figma.setCurrentPageAsync(p);\n  out.push('=== '+p.name);\n  const walk=(n,d)=>{ let s='  '.repeat(d)+n.type+' '+n.id+' \"'+n.name+'\" '+(n.width?Math.round(n.width)+'x'+Math.round(n.height):''); if(n.type==='TEXT') s+=' :: '+n.characters.replace(/\\n/g,' | '); if((n.type==='RECTANGLE'||n.type==='FRAME') && n.fills && n.fills[0] && n.fills[0].type==='SOLID'){const c=n.fills[0].color; s+=' fill#'+[c.r,c.g,c.b].map(v=>Math.round(v*255).toString(16).padStart(2,'0')).join('');} out.push(s); if(n.children) n.children.forEach(c=>walk(c,d+1)); };\n  p.children.forEach(c=>walk(c,0));\n}\nreturn out.join('\\n');"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":26,"cache_creation_input_tokens":970,"cache_read_input_tokens":7916,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":970,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":38,"service_tier":"standard","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1ed87517-1430-4a61-8f00-7b155f170969","uuid":"bdd4b1c6-16c7-4c04-8576-f80037add056","timestamp":"2026-11-03T07:38:13.028Z","tool_use_meta":[{"id":"toolu_bdrk_01wC5yVjhR3ER4I5FWpSPdnN","display_name":"Use Figma","server_display_name":"figma-authenticated-proxy","tool_name":"use_figma"}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01wC5yVjhR3ER4I5FWpSPdnN","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"=== 00 · Start Here 设计任务\nFRAME 6:2 \"Start Here · Brief\" 1440x3368 fill#ffffff\n  FRAME 6:3 \"Header\" 1312x145\n    TEXT 6:4 \"LEVEL L2 · DESIGN TASK · v2\" 182x19 :: LEVEL L2 · DESIGN TASK · v2\n    TEXT 6:5 \"Fitness App — workouts and daily activity\" 1312x52 :: Fitness App — workouts and daily activity\n    TEXT 6:6 \"Design a fitness app: get started, pick a workout or continue today’s plan, explore programs, open a workout to see its rounds, and review today’s activity report. Canvas 390 × 844, iPhone. Work in your own new Figma file — this file is read-only reference.\" 1312x50 :: Design a fitness app: get started, pick a workout or continue today’s plan, explore programs, open a workout to see its rounds, and review today’s activity report. Canvas 390 × 844, iPhone. Work in your own new Figma file — this file is read-only reference.\n  FRAME 6:7 \"How to work\" 1312x227\n    TEXT 6:8 \"How to work\" 147x35 :: How to work\n    TEXT 6:9 \"1. Build exactly the 5 frames below, named exactly as listed (one state per frame), and wire them as a clickable prototype with the listed links. 2. Everything in “Must include” must appear on that frame. The lists are grouped by subject and sorted alphabetically — they are not in screen order and say nothing about layout, grouping, emphasis or styling. Those are your decisions. 3. The two brand colors and the typeface in 01 · Foundations are fixed. Define every other color yourself, plus type scale, spacing, radii and elevation, and apply them consistently. 4. 02 · Components gives only a default Button, a default Text Field and the platform shell (status bar, home indicator). Design all other states, the headers, the navigation and every business component as reusable components in your file. 5. Use the photos, the map and the icons from 04 · Media. 6. Copy and data must match “Fixed data” exactly. This brief wins over anything you may know of the original kit.\" 1312x176 :: 1. Build exactly the 5 frames below, named exactly as listed (one state per frame), and wire them as a clickable prototype with the listed links. | 2. Everything in “Must include” must appear on that frame. The lists are grouped by subject and sorted alphabetically — they are not in screen order and say nothing about layout, grouping, emphasis or styling. Those are your decisions. | 3. The two brand colors and the typeface in 01 · Foundations are fixed. Define every other color yourself, plus type scale, spacing, radii and elevation, and apply them consistently. | 4. 02 · Components gives only a default Button, a default Text Field and the platform shell (status bar, home indicator). Design all other states, the headers, the navigation and every business component as reusable components in your file. | 5. Use the photos, the map and the icons from 04 · Media. | 6. Copy and data must match “Fixed data” exactly. This brief wins over anything you may know of the original kit.\n  FRAME 6:10 \"Frames · goals · must include · links\" 1312x1185\n    TEXT 6:11 \"Frames · goals · must include · links\" 413x35 :: Frames · goals · must include · links\n    TEXT 6:12 \"Frame names are fixed. Must-include lists are grouped by subject and sorted A–Z: they state what is on the screen, never where it goes or how it looks.\" 1312x22 :: Frame names are fixed. Must-include lists are grouped by subject and sorted A–Z: they state what is on the screen, never where it goes or how it looks.\n    FRAME 6:13 \"Frame cards\" 1312x1096\n      FRAME 6:14 \"01_Onboarding\" 644x276 fill#f7f7fa\n        TEXT 6:15 \"01_Onboarding\" 134x26 :: 01_Onboarding\n        TEXT 6:16 \"Goal: Feel motivated and start.\" 596x20 :: Goal: Feel motivated and start.\n        TEXT 6:17 \"MUST INCLUDE\" 84x16 :: MUST INCLUDE\n        TEXT 6:18 \"• Actions: “Get Started” • Copy: “Wherever you are, health 