{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_bdrk_ubjuuq6a2dlpiv4qul7vh5gswkl4ohwmeutpybj7te3fc7zr3hls","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've built all five screens, their components and the prototype in **03 · Workspace**. The account was confirmed as zuohaosheng@tetras.ai, and I didn't change the reference pages (00, 01, 02, 04). I screenshot-checked every screen after building it, and read back all 9 prototype links to confirm they point to the right screens.\n\n**File:** https://www.figma.com/design/7etw0umjivQ6Yi6l5iEkX3/\n**03 · Workspace page ID:** `24:2`\n\n**Screens**\n| Frame | ID | Size |\n|---|---|---|\n| 01_Onboarding | `33:154` | 390×844 |\n| 02_Home | `33:179` | 390×986, scrolls |\n| 03_Explore | `33:334` | 390×1258, scrolls |\n| 04_Workout | `34:401` | 390×1063, scrolls, no tab bar |\n| 05_Analytics | `35:471` | 390×1066, scrolls |\n\nAll the required content, copy and data from the brief are on these frames, using the Lato font, the two brand colors, and the photos, map and icons from 04 · Media. On the scrolling screens, the status bar, tab bar, home indicator and the \"Let's Workout\" button stay fixed while the content scrolls.\n\n**Components** (frame `28:2`, below the screens): a small token sheet listing my colors, type sizes, spacing, corner radii and shadows, plus these reusable components:\n- **Buttons:** CTA Button with Lime and Dark styles, each in Default, Pressed and Disabled. It's built from the provided Button.\n- **Search Bar:** built from the provided Text Field, with the search icon.\n- **Navigation:** Tab Bar with one version per current tab (Home, Explore, Analytics, Profile), Nav Header with a back button, and Day Item in Default and Current.\n- **Cards and rows:** Level Tag (Beginner, Intermediate, Expert), Stat Pill, Stat Chip, Progress Bar (45, 50 and 75%), Popular Workout Card, Plan Row, Program Card (grid and list layouts), Challenge Card, Promo Banner, Round Row (Default and Playing) and Section Title.\n- **Analytics tiles:** Active Calories, Training Time (ring chart), Cycling (map plus a route line I drew), Heart Rate (line chart), Steps, Sleep (bar chart) and Water (cups).\n\nHow states are shown on the screens: the current tab is a lime pill, the current day (T 12) is dark with a lime dot, plan progress is shown as a bar plus a percentage, and the first round (Jumping Jacks, round 1/3) is in the Playing state.\n\n**Prototype** (starts at 01_Onboarding, flow name \"Fitness App\")\n- Get Started → 02_Home\n- Lower Body Training card → 04_Workout (slides in); back → 02_Home (slides out)\n- On 02_Home: Explore tab → 03_Explore, Analytics tab → 05_Analytics\n- On 03_Explore: Home tab → 02_Home, Analytics tab → 05_Analytics\n- On 05_Analytics: Home tab → 02_Home, Explore tab → 03_Explore\n\n**Limitations**\n- Following the brief, these have no links: the Profile tab, search, Hand Training, plan rows, See more, programs, challenges, rounds, Let's Workout, calendar days and report tiles.\n- I added a few small labels the brief doesn't list: \"Explore\" and \"Analytics\" headings, \"Burned today\", \"NOW PLAYING\", and a \"PU\" initials avatar. I also had to invent the Sleep chart bar heights, since the brief says those values are illustrative.\n- The 🔥 and 💪 emoji display in a fallback font, because Lato has no emoji.\n- I haven't played the prototype in Figma's presentation view. The links are confirmed, but the transitions and fixed-on-scroll behaviour aren't tested."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":26,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1362,"cache_read_input_tokens":103090,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1362,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1ed87517-1430-4a61-8f00-7b155f170969","uuid":"6314a943-befa-4b09-97bc-fd09e0d3bace","timestamp":"2026-11-03T07:52:14.940Z"}
